(42277, 449, 245, '<td valign="top">A testament to Canon''s fantastic consumer-grade camera technology! And Myk, of course! :)</td>', 'A testament to Canon''s fantastic consumer-grade camera technology! And Myk, of course! :)', '2002-04-01 01:14:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(42278, 449, 352, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for the kind comments!  To answere a few questions:<br/>* This was taken with my Canon Powershot G2, not that high end of a camera.<br/>* Yes, it would probably look better with more sky above teh top.<br/>* I think the bottom would have looked better there if I''d have gotten the left side not cut off, or if I''d rotated around slightly to get one of the three pieces of the bottom straight on.</td>', 'Thanks everyone for the kind comments!  To answere a few questions:* This was taken with my Canon Powershot G2, not that high end of a camera.* Yes, it would probably look better with more sky above teh top.* I think the bottom would have looked better there if I''d have gotten the left side not cut off, or if I''d rotated around slightly to get one of the three pieces of the bottom straight on.', '2002-04-01 01:15:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(42279, 449, 543, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!  One thing, though; are you sure about that aperture setting?  That''s a pretty huge depth of field for f2.5, even for a digicam.</td>', 'Congratulations!  One thing, though; are you sure about that aperture setting?  That''s a pretty huge depth of field for f2.5, even for a digicam.', '2002-04-01 04:39:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(42280, 449, 1, '<td valign="top">irae-- My Olympus C-700UZ has 2.8.  It''s not so huge.</td>', 'irae-- My Olympus C-700UZ has 2.8.  It''s not so huge.', '2002-04-01 06:44:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(42281, 449, 245, '<td valign="top">I don''t think irae''s referring to the actual size of the aperture, but the amazing depth of field captured at that setting. It looks more like f8 or smaller to me!</td>', 'I don''t think irae''s referring to the actual size of the aperture, but the amazing depth of field captured at that setting. It looks more like f8 or smaller to me!', '2002-04-01 16:54:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(42282, 449, 352, '<td valign="top">Remember, depth of field is a ratio of the distance you are from the object vs the depth provided.  This ratio changes at different mm equivalent ratios.  I''m not sure if it goes up or down, but this was at maximum telephoto (~105 mm equivalent.)  The fStop came from the EXIF data in ACDSee.</td>', 'Remember, depth of field is a ratio of the distance you are from the object vs the depth provided.  This ratio changes at different mm equivalent ratios.  I''m not sure if it goes up or down, but this was at maximum telephoto (~105 mm equivalent.)  The fStop came from the EXIF data in ACDSee.', '2002-04-02 10:37:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(42283, 449, 543, '<td valign="top">Cool.  Did you focus on the top, or somewhere in the middle?</td>', 'Cool.  Did you focus on the top, or somewhere in the middle?', '2002-04-03 09:24:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(42284, 449, 352, '<td valign="top">Exact middle of the picture.  For this I didn''t focus and recompose with prior focus locked.  All I changed was exposure settings to get good lighting.  The contrast of the metal of the Space Needle seems to make it a really good subject for both day and night shooting.  I got a couple more angles the other day during light hours, and they came out fairly similiar in sharpness.</td>', 'Exact middle of the picture.  For this I didn''t focus and recompose with prior focus locked.  All I changed was exposure settings to get good lighting.  The contrast of the metal of the Space Needle seems to make it a really good subject for both day and night shooting.  I got a couple more angles the other day during light hours, and they came out fairly similiar in sharpness.', '2002-04-04 15:20:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(42285, 452, 203, '<td valign="top">Looks like frisco.</td>', 'Looks like frisco.', '2002-03-25 00:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(42286, 452, 270, '<td valign="top">Ouch! Harsh light. Good subject though.</td>', 'Ouch! Harsh light. Good subject though.', '2002-03-25 01:33:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(42287, 452, 215, '<td valign="top">the light on the side is very distracting</td>', 'the light on the side is very distracting', '2002-03-25 07:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(42288, 452, 346, '<td valign="top">too much going on. everything has a yellow/orange tint to it</td>', 'too much going on. everything has a yellow/orange tint to it', '2002-03-25 09:15:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(42289, 452, 447, '<td valign="top">I like what you are showing here, but the curb being crooked throws it off for me. If the curb had been placed in the lower third of the photo, I think the crookedness would have worked better.(You could have kicked that garbage up a little!)</td>', 'I like what you are showing here, but the curb being crooked throws it off for me. If the curb had been placed in the lower third of the photo, I think the crookedness would have worked better.(You could have kicked that garbage up a little!)', '2002-03-25 09:53:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(42290, 452, 325, '<td valign="top">Good shot, the coloring and subject are great.  Decent composition, but I would have straightened out the horizon. The low angle is nice and that piece of plastic on the ground is a nice touch, can''t decide if it''s plastic, a smushed can, or a used condom, but it does add to the picture. The tent is just in the right spot.</td>', 'Good shot, the coloring and subject are great.  Decent composition, but I would have straightened out the horizon. The low angle is nice and that piece of plastic on the ground is a nice touch, can''t decide if it''s plastic, a smushed can, or a used condom, but it does add to the picture. The tent is just in the right spot.', '2002-03-25 15:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(42291, 452, 637, '<td valign="top">Great reality picture</td>', 'Great reality picture', '2002-03-25 16:24:00.000000', NULL, 1),
